<h1>Trim Patches</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p>This command is accessible from <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Scan Data &gt; Trim Patches</b></span>.</p>
<p class="description"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Trim Patches</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command removes the overlapping points on scan data patches at given overlapping distance. It works on entire entity, no matter if the scans are selected wholly or partially.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This function reduces the size of a data set by removing overlapping points from each patch. The number of patches in the data set remains the same but each patch will have less points than before. The resulting data set is in scan data format.</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-left:40px;"><img src="Images/Trim_Patches.gif" width="257px" height="165px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Patches Overlap</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Specifies the maximum overlap area where the points are kept. Default value is 5mm.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Polygon Tolerance</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Specifies patch boundary polygon sampling. Before removing points the overlap area is determined by creating polygon boundary around each patch. Default value is 0.05mm.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
